  "recipe": [
    "Use bounded standard-library subprocess.run for exact manager status with --store, --definition and --verify; capture complete stdout/stderr and real child returncode before checking. Parse whole JSON. Require all Task requiredStatus fields plus exact installed root; output actual exit, stdout byte count/SHA and required identity/validity fields without dumping member inventories. Truncation or parse failure is not verification.",
    "Resolve exact manifest, bootstrap, FRAME_INPUTS, required method owners and helper through the same manager/store/basis. Require exact requested URI, expected confined path, unique standards.members or auxiliary.plugin.members entry and whole-file digest. Helper is auxiliary.plugin scripts/read_basis.py; docs use their actual inventory roots.",
    "Read actual FRAME_INPUTS.frames array and require one id=bootstrap, exact path/bytes/SHA, required binds/routes arrays,1+15 rows and exact selector set below. Each owner/anchor/owner_sha256/section_sha256 must be present. No .get(...,[]) population defaults.",
    "For each of five owner groups, call existing pinned Python -B helper read --stdo MANAGER --store STORE --definition EXACT --member OWNER with one --heading argument per declared exact heading. Each subprocess captured completely and bounded; parse the full JSON. Require actual exit0,status=checked, exact definition/basis/manifest/member digest and exact section headings/count.",
    "Hash every returned section.text and match both its returned sha256 and the corresponding actual FRAME_INPUTS section_sha256; verify owner bytes match owner_sha256. Emit compact16row comparison ledger with exact owner/anchor/heading/line range/digest/result and require completed count16. Selected0 in Results excerpt metadata is legitimate, not a zero-population shortcut.",
    "Existing helper owns fence/comment-safe section projection. REFERENCE_FRAME activation contains fenced headings; no naive heading scanner, improvised replacement or mutable basis. Helper refusal/incomplete returns the concrete cause. Required body reads in Task are separate; byte checks do not acquire source content."
  ],
